  "tagline": "Rust-built cloud data warehouse on object storage, open source with a managed Databend Cloud.",
  "description": "Databend is an open-source, Snowflake-style warehouse written in Rust: stateless compute clusters over data stored in S3-compatible object storage, with elastic scaling and a vectorized engine. It supports a VARIANT type for semi-structured data, time travel, streams for change capture, inverted, vector and spatial indexes, and recently table branching. Databend Cloud is the managed version, and the self-hosted edition is attractive for teams that want a warehouse on their own object storage. Its community is smaller, and stable releases follow a fast-moving nightly train.",
